cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the paper below."
title: "Deep Learning of Robust Market Making under Regime-Switching Order Flow"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Moret"
    given-names: "Felipe"
    affiliation: "Scuola Normale Superiore, Pisa"
  - family-names: "Lillo"
    given-names: "Fabrizio"
    affiliation: "Scuola Normale Superiore, Pisa"
abstract: >-
  A Rainbow-style distributional DQN (C51) market maker, calibrated and tested
  in a zero-intelligence limit order book, that outperforms the
  Guéant-Lehalle-Fernandez-Tapia benchmark across the risk-return frontier and,
  via a Bayesian change-point flow filter, a quote-exposure imbalance signal and
  a scenario-bandit step, stays profitable under regime-switching order flow.
keywords:
  - market making
  - reinforcement learning
  - limit order book
  - regime switching
  - distributional DQN
license: MIT
